'' The calling convention is RECORDED, not merely eaten. It decides the emitted name on
'' win32 -- '_H@4' for stdcall against '_G' for cdecl -- and a definition INHERITS its
'' declaration's, which is why the two must be one symbol.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-symbols tests/symbols/src/callconv.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 'cd' defined cdecl
'' EXPECT-OUT: 'pa' defined pascal
'' EXPECT-OUT: 'inh' declared defined cdecl
'' EXPECT-OUT: 'ec' declared cdecl
'' EXPECT-OUT: 'ew' declared stdcall
